 "style": {
  "name": "Modern Contemporary",
  "summary": "Matched to the concept image: a clean white double-storey volume framed by a bold outer portal, a full-height dark grey slate stone feature pier separating the left car porch/terrace bay from the right living bay, vertical warm teak timber louvers screening the upper master suite, warm wood soffit panels, frameless glass balcony balustrades, and roof solar panels.",
  "materials": [
   "smooth white elastomeric plaster",
   "dark grey split-face slate stone cladding",
   "vertical teak wood louvers and timber soffits",
   "matte black aluminium window frames",
   "frameless tempered glass railings",
   "charcoal flamed granite driveway pavers"
  ],
  "palette": [
   "#f5f3ef",
   "#4f5459",
   "#a86b38",
   "#1e2022",
   "#d8d2c7"
  ]
 },
 "notes": [
  "Setbacks strictly follow LDA 10-marla regulations: 10 ft front, 7 ft rear, and 5 ft right-hand side open space, yielding a 30x48 ft buildable footprint (1,440 sq ft ground coverage = 63.3% \u2264 70%).",
  "Front massing directly reflects the chosen concept image: a 16 ft wide two-car porch on the left topped by a deep glass-railed terrace balcony, and the drawing room and louvered master bedroom on the right.",
  "Ground floor houses two bedrooms at the quiet rear (Parents and Guest rooms with attached baths), a front drawing room accessible from the porch, a main kitchen + dirty kitchen on the right side gallery, and a central double-height TV lounge.",
  "First floor accommodates three bedrooms with attached baths, an upper family lounge overlooking the double-height space via a gallery bridge, an exterior-daylit kitchenette, and a full-size 14x8 ft prayer room along the right open space.",
  "Every bathroom and powder room has direct natural ventilation to the exterior open spaces, and the flat roof slab provides ample area for solar panel arrays alongside the 9.5 ft mumty and concrete overhead water tank."
 ],
